OL,3,GNEWSAStorm-hit families keep 'brave
OL,4,Aface' without power
OL,5,
OL,6,FIt was an unusual start to half term
OL,7,Ffor thousands of families who were left
OL,8,Fwithout power during and after Storm
OL,9,FBoelo.
OL,11,FMany communities across Cumbria
OL,12,Fresorted to camping stoves and
OL,13,Fcandlelit dinners as high winds
OL,14,Fbattered the county at the weekend,
OL,15,Fwhile food vans provided free meals to
OL,16,Fthose worst hit.
OL,18,FKatherine Ord and her four-year-old
OL,19,Fdaughter Eden, from Scotby near
OL,20,FCarlisle, lost power on Saturday
OL,21,Fafternoon and slept with two duvets
OL,22,Feach to keep warm.
OL,23,APub: 27-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB NW Eng NewsC Reg TVF Weather
